From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:16:36 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 192/193] Meridian: git in the Workbench (Source Control)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Workbench page can run git, and gh for pull requests, in the open
project: only the commands the Source Control panel uses (status, diff,
show, add, restore, commit, branch, switch, log, fetch, pull, push…), with
paths inside the project, no option that runs another program or reaches
outside it (-c, -C, --exec, --upload-pack, --output, --ext-diff…), remotes
by name only (no ext:: or file:// addresses), no shell, no prompts, a
timeout and an output cap; fixed safe settings for every run (no fsmonitor,
pager or external diff; ext:: transport off).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
